| phase-40 | `DONE` | B1-NET-01 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-40/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md:814`). New pure-JVM `services/WebDavHrefResolver.kt` origin-resolves every server-supplied PROPFIND `href` (normalized scheme+host+port, default ports materialized, case + trailing-dot folded) and rejects anything that escapes the configured WebDAV server; `WebDavSyncService.kt:147` additionally gates EVERY connection through `requireConfiguredServerOrigin` before the `Authorization: Basic` header is attached (`:164`), and `:158` sets `instanceFollowRedirects=false` so 3xx never forwards credentials/backup bytes (closes the WebDAV slice of B1-NET-05 as well). Off-origin/private-IP/cleartext-downgrade hrefs are `SyncResult(false, "Sync refused: ...")` with a clear message; relative hrefs resolve per RFC 3986 under the request URL. `docs/security-report.md` B1-NET-01 row flipped to `FIXED`. Tests: `WebDavHrefResolverTest` (19, incl. end-to-end PROPFIND-XML cases); `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest` green in isolation and 900/902 green in the full run (2 unrelated flaky failures — `WikiLinkParserCacheUnitTest` + `PluginUpdateEngineTest` timing/cancel cases that pass on re-run and are untouched by this diff), `gradle :app:assembleDebug` green. |
| phase-41 | `DONE` | B1-NET-02 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-41/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md:815`). Confirmed-pairing gate for LocalSend sends. New pure-JVM `services/localsend/LocalSendPairing.kt`: `LocalSendPairing.gate` refuses any receiver that announces `protocol:"http"` (or no TLS fingerprint) and any device whose fingerprint was never paired; `LocalSendPairing.startPairing` derives a deterministic 6-digit out-of-band code (`LocalSendPairingCodes.pairingCode`) + formatted fingerprint; `confirmPairing`/`pair` persist a TOFU anchor (constant-time code compare, `ConstantTime.stringEqual`) into a `LocalSendPairedDeviceStore` (`InMemoryLocalSendPairedDeviceStore` for tests; `SettingsLocalSendPairedDeviceStore` + `SettingsManager.localsend_paired_<fp>` for production). `LocalSendSender` now gates `sendFile` BEFORE any network I/O (`LocalSendSender.kt:313-326`) and pins every payload to the stored paired fingerprint, refuses non-`https` payload URLs in `openConnection`, and the announce never advertises `protocol:"http"` (`LocalSendMessages.senderIdentity` = `"https"`, `LocalSendProtocol.kt:107`). `LocalSendSendDialog` requires an explicit pairing (code typed from the receiver — verified constant-time, mismatch refuses — OR an explicit "fingerprints match" acknowledgement, `LocalSendSendDialog.kt:158-199`) before a device is sendable, and a per-send confirmation before every transmission — a `200` to `/prepare-upload` is documented + treated as ZERO evidence of human consent. Tests: `LocalSendPairingTest` (19) + `LocalSendProtocolTest` (25); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 924 green + `gradle assembleDebug` green (1 pre-existing flaky `PluginUpdateEngineTest` timing failure that passes in isolation — unrelated to this diff, per phase-40 report). |
| phase-42 | `DONE` | B1-NET-03 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-42/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-NET-03 row). Plugin update trust anchor moved into the APK — the manifest can no longer set `downloadUrl`/`sha256`/`pinnedCertHash` out of nothing. New `plugins/runtime/CompileTimePluginPinStore.kt`: per-plugin compile-time release pins (`PinnedPluginRelease` id → version → {sha256, pinnedCertHash}), `PinVerdict`, download-host allow-list (`DEFAULT_DOWNLOAD_HOSTS = {DEFAULT_MANIFEST_HOST}`) with `isHostAllowListed` host gate (lowercase + trailing-dot folded, port ignored), and the production `CompileTimePluginPins.RELEASES` EMPTY ⇒ fail closed (no downloadable plugin shipped yet); all digest compares via `ConstantTime.hexEqual`. Wired as defense-in-depth at THREE independent gates: `PluginUpdateChecker.check` offers only compile-time-pinned values (`plugins/runtime/PluginUpdateChecker.kt`), `PluginUpdateEngine.update` re-verifies the persisted target against pins BEFORE any byte moves or rollback-root write (`plugins/runtime/PluginUpdateEngine.kt:110-116`), and `PluginDownloader` now refuses any artifact host not on the allow-list before connecting (`allowedDownloadHosts` param, `plugins/runtime/PluginDownloader.kt`). `PluginStoreController` threads pins into both check calls (`plugins/store/PluginStoreController.kt`). Surviving `PluginUpdateInfo` carries the compile-time pin digests, not the wire's casing/text. Tests: new `CompileTimePluginPinStoreTest` (10) + new B1-NET-03 cases in `PluginUpdateCheckerTest` (5), `PluginUpdateEngineTest` (1, unpinned/re-pinned refused before any byte moves), `PluginDownloaderTest` (2, host allow-list), `PluginUpdateStoreFlowTest` (1, forged offer refused); the documented flaky `PluginUpdateEngineTest#a hash mismatch…` test was made deterministic (tampered served payload can never match the pin — was zip-timestamp clock-tick dependent). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 943 green + `gradle assembleDebug` green. |
| phase-43 | `DONE` | B1-DB-1 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-43/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-DB-1 row). Corrupt-open classifier narrowed to genuine corruption only: `NoteflowDatabase.kt` `isDatabaseCorruptException` matches `android.database.sqlite.SQLiteDatabaseCorruptException`, `net.zetetic.database.sqlcipher.SQLiteNotADatabaseException`, and the messages "file is not a database"/"malformed"/"database disk image is malformed" — a lock-contention/disk-I/O/ENOSPC `SQLiteException` subclass is NO LONGER classified as corruption, so a transient hiccup can never quarantine a healthy vault. Quarantine no longer auto-creates an empty replacement DB: `SafeSupportSQLiteOpenHelper` rethrows after quarantine and a `throwIfVaultQuarantined` guard fails every further open while the persistent flag is set, so an empty vault is created only after the user's explicit "start fresh". `NoteflowViewModel` surfaces `CorruptionRecoveryScreen` in-session (not just on the next launch), gates the six Room-backed note flows on `authenticated && !corruptionBlocked` (`.catch { emit(emptyList()) }` so a discovery race can't crash a collector), resets+re-runs initialization after start-fresh, and clears the corruption flag after a successful restore so the post-restart open isn't guard-blocked. Tests: new `CorruptionClassifierTest` (10); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 953 green + `gradle assembleDebug` green. |
| phase-44 | `DONE` | B1-DB-4 (HIGH) + B1-AUTH-06 (MEDIUM) fixed — SAME root cause (see `workspace/phase-44/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-DB-4/B1-AUTH-06 rows). Note bodies no longer exist as PLAINTEXT files: the field-encrypted `pages.extractedText` column is the ONLY body store. New pure-JVM `services/NoteBodyVaultPolicy.kt` classifies note-body sources (text/-typed + `.md`/`.txt` only — PDF/image/attachments untouched) and resolves/delete-legacy-file policy. New single write path `NotePageDao.updatePageBody` + `NoteRepository.updatePageBody` (AES-GCM per-record AAD). MainActivity (both layouts) now reads `resolveBodyForDisplay` and saves via new `viewModel.saveMarkdownNoteBody`; the `File.writeText` plaintext editor writes and their NonCancellable plumbing are deleted. Text imports (HomeScreen md/txt/docx, `ImportExportService` HTML/ZIP/Obsidian pass-2) and journal/daily/wiki page creation store `sourceFilePath = null` + body in `extractedText`. Readers (`WikiLinkParser.readFullText`, `BacklinksInspector` convert-to-wikilink, `DocumentTextExtractor`) follow the column. One-time `NoteRepository.migrateLegacyPlaintextNoteBodies` sweeps pre-fix file bodies into the encrypted column then deletes the files (undecryptable pages + failed deletes keep their file; flag `SettingsManager.noteBodyPlaintextMigrated` only set on completion); WAL checkpointed + DB HMAC re-stamped after mutation. `MarkdownPreviewScreen` baseDir falls back to the imports dir so relative markdown images keep resolving. Tests: new `NoteBodyVaultPolicyTest` (12); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 965 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. |
| phase-45 | `DONE` | B1-CRYPTO-02 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-45/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-CRYPTO-02 row). The vault DEK is no longer obtainable without the password: `SecurityService` (`services/SecurityService.kt`) now persists the device-wrapped DEK copy behind an internal `DekDeviceStore` seam (`SharedPrefsDekDeviceStore` = prefs `noteflow_keystore`/`noteflow_sec_dek`; `clear()` uses `commit()`, disk-acknowledged, and drops the stale `dek_auth_required` flag); `readDek()` fails closed (absent or `authRequired=true` blob ⇒ null) and `getOrCreateDek` never mints over an auth-gated blob. Pure-JVM `services/DekAtRestPolicy.kt` (decision table) is wired as `NoteflowViewModel.enforceDekAtRestPolicy()` into `setMasterPassword` (after the wrapped-DEK commit), `changeMasterPassword`, `verifyMasterPassword` (every password unlock), `verifyBiometricsAndUnlock`, and `setBiometricEnabled` — biometrics OFF ⇒ `clearDek()` so the ONLY at-rest wrapper is the password-derived KEK; biometrics ON ⇒ repersist ONLY `authRequired=true`. The pre-fix `setBiometricEnabled(false,…)` non-auth re-wrap is deleted. `SecurityService(context)` call sites → `SecurityService.forDevice(context)` (`NoteflowViewModel.kt:115`, `NoteflowDatabase.kt:345`). Tests: new `DekAtRestPolicyTest` (4) + `B1Crypto02DekAtRestTest` (9, incl. a source-level wiring pin); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 978 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Related-but-out-of-scope: factory re-derive + locked-open gap = B1-AUTH-02 (phase-47), silent DEK re-mint = B1-CRYPTO-05 (phase-64), API 26-29 biometric downgrade = B1-CRYPTO-07 (phase-65) — none touched here. |
| phase-46 | `DONE` | B1-AUTH-01 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-46/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-AUTH-01 row). Downloadable-plugin bytecode can no longer reach the vault DEK in-process — two independent gates. (1) Runtime sandbox: pure-JVM `plugins/runtime/PluginFrameworkClassLoader.kt` becomes the plugin `DexClassLoader`'s parent (`services/AppClassLoaderFactory.kt:34`); `isAppPrivateForbidden` (`:70-71`) refuses EVERY `com.authorss81.noteflow.*` class outside the `plugins.*` framework surface (incl. `Class.forName` reach-through), while `java.*`/`kotlin.*`/`android.*`/third-party classes still delegate. (2) Verify-time content gate: pure-JVM `plugins/runtime/ArtifactStaticScan.kt` runs inside `ArtifactSignatureVerifier.verify` (`:76-81`), the single funnel for install / every load re-verify / update / rollback; it structurally parses `.class` constant pools + DEX `string_ids`/`type_ids` and byte-searches other entries, rejecting app-private prefixes (`services|data|ui|theme|utils`), bare secret-bearing names (`VaultKeyHolder`, `EncryptionService`, `NoteflowDatabase`, `SettingsManager`, `NoteRepository`, `SecurityService`) and raw `java.net`/`javax.net.ssl` egress primitives. Phase-46 review closed all 5 review findings in-tree: net-egress + `ProcessBuilder`/`Runtime` now matched in slash AND dot form (`Class.forName("java.net.HttpURLConnection")` literals refused), sensitive names matched ONLY as whole tokens (benign lookalike identifiers pass), and a source-level pin (`PluginBytecodeIsolationTest`) holds that `plugins.*` host code never references a vault-handle type. Tests: `PluginBytecodeIsolationTest` (20); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1001 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Out-of-scope (documented): native `System.loadLibrary`, `sun.misc.Unsafe` and a separate `:remote` process option.
| phase-47 | `DONE` | B1-AUTH-02 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-47/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-AUTH-02 row). The lock is now enforced at the DATA LAYER. `NoteflowViewModel.lock()` (`NoteflowViewModel.kt:2543-2549`) — when a master password exists — now cancels the section/page observer jobs, calls `NoteflowDatabase.dispose()` (closes + forgets the Room/SQLCipher instance so NO keyed handle survives; previously it zeroized only `VaultKeyHolder`), marks `databaseDisposedByLock`, and resets `dataInitialized` so the next unlock re-establishes observers. The stale-handle/fresh-open exploits both fail closed: a stale handle hits a closed connection pool, and `NoteflowSqlcipherFactory.create` (`NoteflowDatabase.kt:343-371`) routes the `dek == null` open through the new pure-JVM `services/LockedOpenGuard.kt` — a password-protected vault with no in-memory DEK THROWS `IllegalStateException("Vault is locked: database key not available")` BEFORE any `getOrCreateDek()`/persisted-copy access, while a passwordless vault still re-reads its device-wrapped copy (the boot credential by design). Explicit unlocks (`verifyMasterPassword` `:2080`, `verifyBiometricsAndUnlock` `:2220`) reinstate the live connection via `reinstateDatabaseAfterLock()` (no-op unless lock() disposed it) BEFORE the dbGate flows flip on, and an open failure there is zeroized and returned — never counted as a wrong password. `onCleared()` also disposes. Tests: `LockedOpenGuardTest` (3) + `B1Auth02LockedOpenTest` (9, incl. a fake-repository model proving no key is ever re-created on a locked open + source-level wiring pins); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1013 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green + `gradle assembleRelease` green. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Related-but-out-of-scope: in-flight save writes with zeroized key = B2-UI-1 (phase-49), plugin lifecycle hooks running before unlock = B1-AUTH-03 (phase-67). |
| phase-48 | `DONE` | B2-LOG-01 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-48/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-LOG-01 row). Crash logging is single-owner. `utils/AppStartupLogger.kt` is a startup-EVENT timer only: the crash handler it installed at `:38-42` (which ran OUTERMOST = FIRST because MainActivity registers PrivacyCrashReporter first) and the raw `logCrash`/`printStackTrace` → `Log.e` dump at `:55-77` are deleted, and the `Log.e(TAG, msg, e)` failure paths (which would print an exception's trace) no longer pass the exception object (`appendToFile` `:61`, `clearLogs` `:86`). `services/PrivacyCrashReporter.kt` is the SOLE `UncaughtExceptionHandler`; its `logUncaughtException` (`:53-55`) routes through the new pure-JVM `crashLogEntry` (`:64-71`, sanitized message + scrubbed `class.method(file:line)` frames, no raw trace) and writes to the local file only — never logcat. Repo-wide source pin: `setDefaultUncaughtExceptionHandler` appears only in `PrivacyCrashReporter.kt`. Tests: new `B2Log01CrashReportingTest` (6, incl. sanitization/scrub behavior + source pins); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1019 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (first invocation had an unreproducible transient failure; all re-invocations fully `UP-TO-DATE` green with the 173.6 MB debug APK on disk). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Out-of-scope (documented): `app_startup.log` size cap/rotation = B2-LOG-02 (phase-70); B1-PLAT-5 (path-regex namespace gap) was planned for phase-89 but CLOSED in this phase's review fix — `sanitizeMessage` now redacts any `/data/user/<uid>/...` or `/data/data/...` path (covers namespace + real applicationId dir), pinned by a new test. |
| phase-49 | `DONE` | B2-UI-1 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-49/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-UI-1 row). Post-lock editor saves can no longer persist PLAINTEXT into field-encrypted columns. The write path fails closed at the data layer: new pure-JVM `services/VaultWriteGate.kt` (`requireKey` throws `VaultLockedWriteException` on a zeroized DEK; `persistNow` = the persist-vs-defer decision) + `services/EditorFlushPolicy.kt` (latest-wins-per-page `DeferredSave` stash, `defer`/`drain`). `NoteRepository.kt` now uses `requireEncryptionKey()` (`:44`) in every encrypted-column write — `updatePageBody` `:409`, `createPage` `:547`, `renamePage` `:574`, `updatePageTitleAndTags` `:587`, `saveStrokesForPage` `:762`, `saveMediaEmbedsForPage` `:905`, `createNoteVersion` `:986` — and the `?: rawTitle/rawExtracted/rawText` and `else { rawText/pointsJson }` elvis/else plaintext fallbacks are grep-verified gone. `NoteflowViewModel.kt` routes every editor page-write through the gate (`flushEditorPageSave` `:2302`, `autosaveStrokes` `:2325`, `saveLayersGated` `:2341`, private `persistOrDefer` `:2362`), stashes locked flushes instead of dropping them, re-writes them ENCRYPTED via `flushPendingEditorSaves()` (`:2395`) in BOTH unlock paths (`:2120`, `:2242`), rejects `createNoteVersion` (`:2275`) while locked, and guards the page-create/rename/language-tag/daily/wiki paths. `EditorScreen.kt` has zero direct `viewModel.repository.save*` call sites left — dispose-flush `:430`, debounced autosave `:505`, layer/embed/sticky/insert-site changes, BackHandler `:857` and the top-bar back `:884` all route via the VM gate; `NonCancellable` import removed. Tests: new `B2Ui1LockedFlushTest` (15 after the review fix, behavior + source pins); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1035 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (transient first-invocation failures in phases 47–49; the phase-49 review-fix run was green on first invocation). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Review fix (2026-08-15): the eight guarded page-write paths (`applyWorkspaceTemplate`/`addPage`/`createNoteFromSharedContent`/`renamePage`/`updatePageTitleAndTags`/`autoTagLanguageOnSave`/`openOrCreateDailyNote`/`openPageByTitle`) now route through `writeGuardedAgainstLock`/`isLockRacedWrite` so a lock racing them is a non-alarming snackbar, never a crash; `saveMarkdownNoteBody` defers lock-beaten bodies via `EditorFlushPolicy.DeferredBody` (`deferBody`/`drainBodies`) and re-writes them encrypted after unlock; `createNoteVersion` lock-rejection shows a notice; in-memory-deferral process-kill trade-off documented. Out-of-scope (documented): clipboard-scrub-on-lock = B2-UI-2, `lastSavedStrokeHash` concurrency = B2-UI-3, unlock state re-init = B2-UI-4, markdown non-atomic writes = B2-UI-5 — none touched here. |
| phase-50 | `DONE` | B2-DOS-01 (HIGH) fixed (see `workspace/phase-50/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-DOS-01 row). Stroke geometry is now bounded at EVERY hop between DB bytes and the composable. New pure-JVM `services/StrokeGeometryPolicy.kt` owns the budgets (MAX_POINTS_PER_STROKE=20k, MAX_POINTS_PER_PAGE=200k, MAX_STROKES_PER_PAGE=2k, plaintext cap 2.5M chars/stroke, stored base64-ciphertext cap 3.4M chars/stroke — AES-GCM does not compress so ciphertext length is an exact proxy) + `applySaveGate`/`gateStroke`/`capLoadedPoints`/`storedPointsJsonOverBudget`/`plaintextPointsJsonOverBudget`. `NoteRepository.saveStrokesForPage` (`:793`, was `:533-587` in the finding) routes EVERY write through the gate and returns a `StrokeGeometryGateResult`; `getStrokesForPage` (`:636`) now pages through the new `StrokeDao.getStrokesForPageBounded` (`Daos.kt:181`, `WHERE length(pointsJson) <= :maxStoredChars … LIMIT :limit OFFSET :offset`), refuses over-budget plaintext before Gson, caps legacy over-specified strokes via `capLoadedPoints`, and stops once the page budget is exhausted — a 2M-point backup stroke can no longer OOM/ANR page-open. `EncryptionService.deserializeStrokes` (`:470`) refuses oversized plaintext pre-parse. `ImportExportService.sanitizeRestoredStrokeGeometry` (`:1674`) DELETEs over-budget stroke rows from a restored DB before re-key/migrate/transplant, so a crafted backup can never land a huge geometry (B1-DB-7 vector). `NoteflowViewModel` surfaces ONE non-alarming snackbar per page per session via `maybeNotifyGeometryCapped` (latch cleared on lock) on all three stroke-save paths. `AnnotationCanvas.kt:1415-1434` culls pages whose slab does not intersect the visible world rect `(screen − pan)/zoom` in paginated mode (paper/template/strokes of off-viewport pages are never drawn) — plus the existing `LayerBitmapCache` already provides the off-main raster for committed strokes. Tests: new `B2Dos01StrokeGeometryTest` (18, incl. source-level wiring pins); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1053 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (first invocation had an unreproducible transient Gradle daemon failure; re-runs fully green. 173.6 MB debug APK on disk). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched.

| phase-51 | `DONE` | B1-NET-04 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-51/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-NET-04 row). SSRF blocklist for Web Capture + Citation title-fetch. New pure-JVM `services/SsrfHostPolicy.kt`: `blockedReason` (`:30`) blocks localhost/`*.local`/`*.localhost`, IPv4 literals in EVERY textual form (dotted-quad, short `127.1`, decimal `2130706433`, hex `0x7f000001`) across `0.0.0.0/8`, RFC-1918, `100.64/10` CGNAT, `127/8`, `169.254/16` (cloud metadata), IPv6 `::`/`::1`, `fe80::/10` link-local, `fc00::/7` ULA (incl. IMDSv2 `fd00:ec2::254`), and IPv4-mapped/compatible embedded forms (`::ffff:192.168.0.1`) — all structural, NO DNS. `WebPageFetchPolicy.validateUrl` (`:58-65`) refuses blocked hosts at entry + new `rejectHop` (`:80`) re-validates every redirect target; `WebPageFetcher.doFetch` (`:32-54`) applies it on EVERY hop AND fixes the pre-existing "redirect never assigned `cur`" bug (`cur = resolved`), keeping the 5-hop cap; `HttpsTitleFetcher.fetch` (rewritten `:39`) now manually follows up to 5 redirects (`instanceFollowRedirects=false`, `:69`), re-checks scheme+hostlist on every hop (HTTPS→HTTP hop refused under default `httpsOnly=true`), and refuses internal hosts/`ftp`/malformed before any socket; `CitationFormatterCore.validateUrl` (`:26-46`) switched to URI host extraction + the same blocklist at entry. Tests: new `B1Net04SsrfBlocklistTest` (19 — policy/entry/hop/fetch-refusal, all no-network); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1072 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (transient first-invocation daemon flake; retry clean, 173.6 MB debug APK on disk). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Out-of-scope (documented): recursive DNS-resolution/rebinding egress pinning (transport-level, future phase), `httpsOnly` optional HTTP kept for citation fallback parity, other B1-NET findings untouched. Review fixes (2026-08-15): ambiguous IPv4 textual encodings (`0x7f.0.0.1`, `0177.0.0.1`) are now refused outright via `SsrfHostPolicy.isOpaqueIpv4Literal`; bare `host:port` inputs are defanged in `normalize`; `WebCaptureEngine.captureWebPage` now fetches the validated/normalized `Validation.url` instead of the raw paste (bare-host captures reach the network). Residual name-based DNS-rebinding (`metadata.google.internal`, `*.nip.io`) documented as tracked out-of-scope in `docs/security-report.md`. `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1075 green (0 failures) + `assembleDebug` green. |

| phase-52 | `DONE` | B1-NET-05 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-52/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-NET-05 row). HTTPS→HTTP redirect downgrades are closed at EVERY base `HttpURLConnection` transport. New pure-JVM `services/StrictRedirectPolicy.kt` is the single hop policy: `checkTlsHop` refuses any hop — entry URL AND every resolved 3xx `Location` — whose scheme is not `https` or whose host fails the B1-NET-04 `SsrfHostPolicy` blocklist; `resolveNextTlsHop` resolves RFC-3986, rejects loops/malformed/blank targets; `MAX_REDIRECTS = 5`. Previously auto-following transports are now `instanceFollowRedirects = false` + manual loop: `DuckDuckGoClient.search` (`DuckDuckGoClient.kt:163`), `OpenMeteoClient.get` (`WeatherClient.kt:104`), `DictionaryClient.lookup` (`DictionaryClient.kt:69`) and `AppFacadeHost.httpGet` (`AppFacadeHost.kt:67` — was `instanceFollowRedirects = true`). Connection factories are constructor-injectable (default = `openConnection`) so each transport is behavior-tested with a fake `HttpURLConnection`. Already-safe transports are source-pinned (`PinnedTlsConnector` plugin transports, `WebDavSyncService`, Web Capture/Citation fetchers) and `LocalSendSender.openConnection` (`LocalSendSender.kt:512`) got the same `= false` for its pinned payload connections. Out-of-scope (documented): `plugins/llm` `AssistantModelDownloader.kt:72` (`= true`) is a separate non-base downloadable-module artifact whose build is outside this phase's verification commands — same one-line treatment needed there before that module ships. Tests: new `B1Net05RedirectDowngradeTest` (28 — policy, per-transport downgrade/blocked/loop/cap, same-scheme https follow, facade, offline-fallback, source pins + repo-wide no-`= true` scan); `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest` 1103 green (0 failures) + `gradle :app:assembleDebug` green. Review fixes (2026-08-15): the last base-app redirect-following hole was closed — `LocalSendSender.httpRegisterProbe` (`:235`) now sets `instanceFollowRedirects = false` (`:240`; it was missed by the initial sweep because the string-pin only proved the file contained *some* `= false`); the source-pin test now enforces a per-file count invariant (every `openConnection()` must be matched by an `instanceFollowRedirects = false`, class now 29 tests), closing the LocalSend gap and catching any future un-paired `openConnection()`; `AppFacadeHost` hop-cap wording unified to `"redirected too many times"` (`AppFacadeHost.kt:98`); trailing newline restored on `StrictRedirectPolicy.kt`. Re-run: `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest` 1104 green (0 failures) + `gradle :app:assembleDebug` green. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. |
| phase-53 | `DONE` | B1-DB-2 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-53/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-DB-2 row). The plaintext→SQLCipher migration no longer deletes the original plaintext database on ANY failure. `NoteflowDatabase.migratePlaintextIfNeeded` (`NoteflowDatabase.kt:201-258`) now swaps atomically: the encrypted scratch file is verified (exists, non-empty, no plaintext header — `isPlaintextSqlite(tempFile) || tempFile.length() == 0L` → throw) and `tempFile.renameTo(dbFile)` replaces the original via `rename()` (atomic on bionic/Linux), removing the delete-then-rename window in which the user had NO database file; the stale `-wal`/`-shm` companions are removed only AFTER the verified encrypted file is in place. The catch block no longer deletes db+wal+shm — it routes through the new pure-JVM `quarantineMigrateFailed` (`NoteflowDatabase.kt:487-510`, `internal fun`, File-only): drops ONLY the scratch copy, preserves the original + `-wal`/`-shm`/`-journal` as `noteflow.sqlite.migrate-failed-<ts>` (bytes preserved, mirroring the phase-09 `*.corrupt-<ts>` quarantine), returns the timestamp for `DatabaseSecurityHelper.setCorruptionDetected`, and then `throw e` — the phase-43 `initializeData` catch spot-checks that flag in-session and surfaces the corruption-recovery screen (restore from backup / explicit start fresh). Tests: new `B1Db02MigrationFailureTest` (7 — behaviors: bytes preserved under `*.migrate-failed-*` incl. companions, missing companions/scratch handled, timestamp==suffix; source pins: catch routes through quarantine + sets the flag + rethrows, no `dbFile.delete()` in the catch, the only live-db delete is the empty-stub guard, swap-before-cleanup ordering). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1111 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (first invocation had an unreproducible transient build failure; retry fully green with the 173.6 MB debug APK on disk). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. |
| phase-55 | `DONE` | B1-DB-5 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-55/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-DB-5 row). HTML/Obsidian ZIP imports now fail zebrabomb-like archives cleanly with bounded heap. New pure-JVM `services/ImportArchivePolicy.kt` owns the budgets (per-entry 50MB `MAX_IMPORT_ENTRY_BYTES`, total 200MB `MAX_IMPORT_TOTAL_BYTES`, 100× declared-vs-actual expansion ratio with 4KB floor, entry count 10k `MAX_IMPORT_ENTRY_COUNT`, 200MB archive input) and the exact single-settle accounting (`checkEntryChunk` never mutates; `settleEntryRead` once per completed entry — the first implementation double-counted the cumulative entryBytes per chunk and was caught by the new test) + `ImportSizeLimitException` (an `IllegalStateException`) so every rejection surfaces a clean non-alarming message. `ImportExportService.readUriBytes` (`:89-118`) reads under a hard stream cap and re-throws the dedicated exception (never swallowed by the null-on-error catch); `importHtmlZipOrFolder` (`:2063`) and `importObsidianVaultZip` (`:2250`, refactored to a SINGLE pass so accounting is exact and entries parse once) route every entry through `claimEntry`/`readEntryBounded` + `inputArchiveOverLimit`; `importHtmlFile` rethrows; the `zis.readBytes()` calls are gone repo-wide (source-pinned). `MAX_BACKUP_INPUT_BYTES` (`:1137`) is now public and the two restore callers (`HomeScreen.kt:148`, `NoteflowViewModel.kt:1805`) keep the 400MB backup cap so large legitimate vaults still restore; `Dialogs.kt:96` APK picker bounded to 400MB. HomeScreen `processImportedUris` surfaces `"Import skipped: …"` for oversized/bombed archives instead of a silent skip. Tests: new `B1Db05ImportZipBombTest` (13 — incl. a REAL 60MB-of-zeros zip that stops at ~50MB with `totalBytes <= 50MB+8192`, a 101-entry archive vs 100-budget, ratio triple, total, happy-path round-trip, source pins); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1142 green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (173.6MB debug APK, SHA-256 `ece3d77b…`). |

| phase-56 | `DONE` | B1-DB-7 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-56/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-DB-7 row). The legacy restore path can no longer accept an attacker-crafted PLAIN (unencrypted) zip nor open a backup's SQLCipher DB with the empty passphrase. Two pure-JVM gates in `ImportExportService.kt` (file-level `internal fun`s, both pinned by tests): `isPlainPkBackupBytes` classifies a raw `PK`-headed payload, and `backupRestoreOpenCandidates` returns ONLY `listOfNotNull(backupDekHex, currentDekHex).filter { it.isNotBlank() }.distinct()` — the historic `""` empty-key entry is gone AND stripped fail-closed even if a future caller passes it. `importBackup` (`:1595-1600`) REJECTS the plain zip outright with `"Restore rejected: this is an unencrypted (unsigned) backup."` BEFORE any decrypt/extract (the app has not produced keyless backups since the H4 fix, so nothing legitimate is lost); the authenticated device-DEK-encrypted legacy path (`:1601-1608`) and the NFLB2 password-v2 path are untouched. `validateAndPrepareRestoredDb` (`:1692`, candidate line `:1699`) now consumes only `backupRestoreOpenCandidates`, so an attacker's empty-passphrase `noteflow.sqlite` can never pass `PRAGMA integrity_check` and be re-keyed + HMAC-rearmed + swapped over the live vault. `HomeScreen.kt` picker (`:160-176`) refuses a PK zip with a non-alarming snackbar before any confirm dialog, and the remaining device-keyed legacy confirm dialog (`:1138-1147`) now explicitly warns the backup is UNTRUSTED/UNSIGNED. Tests: new `B1Db07PlainZipRestoreRejectedTest` (12 — PK classifier behavior, candidate-set fail-closed incl. `""`/blank inputs, no-duplicate/empty-set, source pins for the two gates + the picker refusal + the dialog warning); `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1154 green (0 failures, 1142 + 12) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (full `--rerun-tasks` recompile with no `e:` errors, 173.7 MB debug APK SHA-256 `4b025ea4…`; the first invocation had a transient build failure, the forced clean re-run is fully green). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. |
| phase-59 | `DONE` | B1-PLAT-3 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-59/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-PLAT-3 row). Whole-vault/plaintext exports no longer auto-write to the world-readable public Downloads. Chose the finding's "better" fix (SAF rewrite): (1) the six `Environment.getExternalStoragePublicDirectory(DIRECTORY_DOWNLOADS)` copies in `ImportExportService.kt` and the one in `PsdExportService.kt` are deleted — every export wrapper keeps its output app-private in `cacheDir`; (2) every user-facing export routes through the new reusable `ui/components/SaFExporter.kt` (`rememberSaFExporter`) which delivers bytes via `ACTION_CREATE_DOCUMENT` (MIME + suggested name from the pure-JVM `services/ExportDestinationPolicy.kt` decision table) and deletes the staging copy on success (transfer-then-delete; API 19+, below minSdk 26, no fallback needed); (3) the whole-vault PLAINTEXT kinds (`OBSIDIAN_VAULT`/`HTML_SITE`/`VAULT_ZIP`) gate the picker behind a bold red "Export is NOT encrypted" consent dialog; (4) HomeScreen (plain backup, password backup, Obsidian, HTML site, notebook/section vault zips) + EditorScreen (PNG, WebP, page PDF, document PDF, note HTML, PSD, section vault zip) all rerouted through `exporter.export(...)` with the correct `ExportKind`; all "saved to Downloads" snackbars gone; LocalSend's cacheDir payload path intentionally unchanged. Tests: new `ExportDestinationPolicyTest` (11) + `B1Plat03ExportConsentTest` (5, source pins incl. a comment-stripped repo-wide no-`getExternalStoragePublicDirectory` scan). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1196 total with the only 2 failures pre-existing `B1Plat01ReleaseSigningTest` asserts on `docs/RELEASE.md`/`app/build.gradle.kts` (proven unrelated by failing identically on a clean stashed tree); `gradle assembleDebug` green (173.7 MB debug APK; the first invocation had an unrelated transient build failure — retry + final run green). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. |
| phase-60 | `DONE` | B1-PLAT-4 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-60/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-PLAT-4 row). Auto-lock is no longer OFF by default and no longer fires only on full backgrounding / next-touch. New pure-JVM `services/AutoLockPolicy.kt` owns `DEFAULT_AUTO_LOCK_TIMEOUT_SECONDS = 300` (SettingsManager reads it), `shouldAutoLock` (>= boundary, 0/negative = disabled) and `IDLE_CHECK_INTERVAL_MS`; `MainActivity` runs a continuous 1 s idle poll while authenticated (`LaunchedEffect(autoLockTimeoutSeconds, authenticated)`), stamps a fresh baseline at each unlock, keeps the pointerInput touch handler timestamp-only (never a lock decision), locks instantly on `ACTION_SCREEN_OFF` via a runtime receiver (register in onCreate, deregister in onDestroy; API 33+ uses the flagged registration, the plain system-broadcast registration below that), and applies FLAG_SECURE unconditionally (the debug clearFlags carve-out is deleted). `ON_STOP` → lock retained; `ON_PAUSE`→lock explicitly NOT chosen (breaks SAF pickers / biometric / share-sheet pauses). Tests: `B1Plat04AutoLockTest` (10 — pure-JVM decision + wiring source pins). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1206 total with only the 2 pre-existing `B1Plat01ReleaseSigningTest` failures (`docs/RELEASE.md`/build.gradle signing asserts, untouched); `gradle assembleDebug` green (173.7 MB debug APK, SHA-256 `d2c2eae7…`). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. |
| phase-61 | `DONE` | B1-PLAT-7 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-61/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-PLAT-7 row). Locally-present APKs are never a trusted update source and public Downloads are no longer scanned. New pure-JVM `services/UpdateTrustPolicy.kt` owns the decision table: `classifySource`/`hasOfficialChannel` → every local APK is `UNTRUSTED_LOCAL` (no official channel, no remote-verified signing key); `isPubliclyWritableDirectory` structurally refuses `/sdcard`, `/storage/emulated`, and `…/Android/data/…` external-files-dir mounts (case-insensitive, slash-normalized); `isScanSafeDirectory` gates every scan candidate; `mayInstall` fail-closed-gates UNTRUSTED installs behind explicit confirmation; trust-neutral announcement/confirmation copy (never "New update detected"). `UpdateService.checkForDownloadedUpdates` (`UpdateService.kt:128`) now scans ONLY app-private `filesDir`/`cacheDir` through the policy filter (the `getExternalFilesDir` + `/sdcard/Download` + `/storage/emulated/0/Download` scan dirs at `:104-137` are deleted); `inspectApkFile` (`:60`) classifies via the policy and drops the conditioning wording; `installApk` (`:175`) gained `trust` + `userConfirmedUntrusted` and its FIRST check is `UpdateTrustPolicy.mayInstall` — an untrusted file without confirmation is refused before any staging/FileProvider/launch. `AppUpdateDialog` (`ui/components/Dialogs.kt`) relabeled to "Scan App Storage for APK", never says "Downloads", and gates "Install Update" behind the strong untrusted-confirmation dialog (`Install anyway` / `Cancel`, error colour) invoking `installApk` only with `userConfirmedUntrusted = true`. Tests: `B1Plat07UpdateTrustTest` (11 test methods — pure-JVM decision table + source pins incl. repo-scan for the removed public-dir literals). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1217 total with only the 2 pre-existing `B1Plat01ReleaseSigningTest` failures (untouched `docs/RELEASE.md`/build.gradle asserts, documented in phases 55/59/60 too); `gradle assembleDebug` green. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Scope: signature equality demoted to integrity-hint only (B1-PLAT-1 key rotation = phase-57); no official network update channel exists — when one ships it must use remote-verified pins, never a local APK feed. |
| phase-62 | `DONE` | B1-CRYPTO-03 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-62/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-CRYPTO-03 row). The salt + wrapped-DEK are no longer written as two independent SharedPreferences `.apply()` writes (`NoteflowViewModel.kt:1794-1795/1829-1830`) whose inter-write kill permanently bricked the vault. New pure-JVM `services/MasterPasswordCredential.kt` makes the pair ONE versioned blob (`MPB1|<saltB64>|<wrappedDek>`, `serialize`/`parse`/`fromLegacy`; `parse` fails closed on malformed/half values) — pure JVM (`java.util.Base64`) so the atomicity contract is unit-testable. `SettingsManager.commitMasterPasswordCredential` (`SettingsManager.kt:101`) persists blob + removes the two legacy keys in ONE synchronous disk-sync `commit()` (SharedPreferences' atomic temp-file+rename => a torn write leaves the PREVIOUS complete blob — a half pair is structurally impossible) and returns the disk-acked result; the read accessor `masterPasswordCredentialOrLegacy` (`:84`) prefers the blob and falls back to the legacy two-key pair, so pre-fix vaults keep unlocking until the next set/change migrates them (same atomic commit). `NoteflowViewModel.setMasterPassword` (`:2094`) / `changeMasterPassword` (`:2145`) round-trip-validate the wrapped DEK (`EncryptionService.decrypt(wrapped, derivedKek)`, zeroized check buffer) BEFORE committing and abort (`return false`) before any in-memory state flips when the commit fails; `verifyMasterPassword` (`:2211`) + `unwrapMasterDek` (`:2272`) read the credential through the single accessor. `clearSecuritySettings` also drops the blob. No DB schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Tests: new `B1Crypto03MasterPasswordAtomicTest` (7 — blob round-trip + fail-closed parse, torn-write leaves old credential durable/unlockable, a store dying on the SECOND write (the audit fault injection) refuses the change and never bricks the vault, torn-position sweep invariant, legacy-pair resolution, source pins for single-commit/round-trip/no-two-pref-writes/accessor reads). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1224 total with only the 2 pre-existing `B1Plat01ReleaseSigningTest` failures (untouched `docs/RELEASE.md`/build.gradle asserts, documented in phases 55/59/60/61); `gradle assembleDebug` green (173.7 MB debug APK, SHA-256 `e463a944…`; first invocation hit the documented transient dex-merge failure — retry green). |
| phase-63 | `DONE` | B1-CRYPTO-04 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-63/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-CRYPTO-04 row). A NEW master password must now clear the pure-JVM `services/PasswordStrengthPolicy.kt` (the single decision table, KDoc documents the finding's "lockout is UI-only / vault only as strong as the password" caveat + Argon2id/TEE follow-ups): `PasswordStrengthVerdict` (ACCEPTED/TOO_SHORT/TOO_LONG/SEQUENTIAL/WEAK/LOW_DIVERSITY, each with a human-readable message) + `evaluate` = ≥ 8 NFKC-normalized graphemes (`MIN_STRENGTH_GRAPHEMES`, stronger than the old 6 floor, ≤ the 128 cap) + no sequential/keyboard-row/single-run-repeat patterns (`12345678`, `qwerty`, `1qaz2wsx`, `aaaaaaaa`, `abab…`) + ≥ 3 distinct graphemes + (for < 12 graphemes) ≥ 3 of 4 classes (upper/lower/digit/symbol); passphrases ≥ 12 pass on length alone so `correct horse battery staple` is accepted. Measured on `EncryptionService.normalizePassword` (the exact bytes `deriveKey` hashes, B2-CRYPTO-07) — full-width `１２３４５６７８` folds to `12345678` and is rejected as sequential. Enforced as the authoritative gate in `NoteflowViewModel.setMasterPassword` (`:2071`) + `changeMasterPassword` (`:2134`, NEW password only; the OLD password stays verify-only so pre-existing weaker vaults keep unlocking and rotating) and surfaced with `verdict.message` by both Dialogs.kt master-password dialogs (set `:682`, change `:631`). Repo pin: `PasswordStrengthPolicy` is referenced only by the policy file, the ViewModel gate and Dialogs.kt; unlock paths (`verifyMasterPassword`/`unwrapMasterDek`/`isMasterPasswordValid`) never strength-gate. No DB schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Tests: new `B1Crypto04PasswordStrengthTest` (10 — rejected short/sequential/keyboard/repeated/low-diversity sets, NFKC folding, accepted set, passphrase exception, source pins incl. a repo-wide no-leak scan). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1239 total with only the 2 pre-existing `B1Plat01ReleaseSigningTest` failures (proven unrelated on a clean stashed tree, as in phases 55/59/60/61/62); `gradle assembleDebug` green. |
| phase-65 | `DONE` | B1-CRYPTO-07 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-65/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-CRYPTO-07 row). The vault-DEK biometric AndroidKeyStore key was only `AUTH_BIOMETRIC_STRONG`-bound on API 30+ (`SecurityService.kt:38-45`); on API 26-29 the bare `setUserAuthenticationRequired(true)` path left the key satisfiable by a screen PIN/pattern/password (AOSP pre-30 maps any non-(-1) validity, incl. default 0, to `HW_AUTH_PASSWORD | HW_AUTH_BIOMETRIC`). New pure-JVM `services/BiometricKeyBindingPolicy.kt` = single decision table (`MIN_API_FOR_STRONG_BIOMETRIC_BINDING = 30`, `strongBiometricKeyBindingSupported`, `refuseEnableMessage`, `PRE_30_BIOMETRIC_ONLY_VALIDITY_SECONDS = -1`). Enforcement: `NoteflowViewModel.setBiometricEnabled` (`:2531`) REFUSES enabling below API 30 (one-shot non-alarming `biometricRefusalMessage` StateFlow `:1106`) before the setting flips; `enforceDekAtRestPolicy` (`:2194`) DOWNGRADES a legacy enabled state below API 30 to password-only (setting off + `clearDek()`, never re-writes the weak-bound copy); `SecurityService.getOrCreateKey` (`:76-98`) binds any pre-30 auth key defensively with `setUserAuthenticationValidityDurationSeconds(-1)` (biometric-only per use) instead of the bare-required path; `getDecryptionCipher` (`:105-127`) + `NoteflowViewModel.getBiometricCipher` (`:2579`) return null below API 30 so LockScreen falls back to the master password + `disableBiometricFallback()`. The finding's explicit API-level marker: `storeDek` stamps `DekDeviceBlob.wrapperApiLevel = Build.VERSION.SDK_INT` (`dek_wrapper_api_level` in `SharedPrefsDekDeviceStore`) — informational/auditable only, NOT read-gated (pre-fix API-30+ blobs carry marker 0 and must still unlock). `BiometricAuthHelper` now distinguishes availability (`isBiometricAvailable`) from strong-bindability (`canCreateStrongBiometricBoundKey`); the settings dialog (`Dialogs.kt:502`) gates the switch on the latter. `DekAtRestPolicy.modeFor` gained `strongBiometricBindingSupported: Boolean = true` (default keeps 2-arg call sites compatible). Out of scope, documented in REPORT.md §8: `WebDavCredentialStore`'s positive-duration pre-30 binding (B1-NET-08 design) and the minSdk-30 bump (product decision). No DB schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Tests: new `B1Crypto07BiometricKeyBindingTest` (20 — policy decision table, downgrade, source pins for the binding branches/API marker/cipher gates/UI wiring). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1275 total with only the 2 pre-existing `B1Plat01ReleaseSigningTest` failures (verified identical on a clean stash; documented in phases 55/59/60/61/62/63/64); `gradle assembleDebug` green (173.7 MB debug APK, SHA-256 `d571b695d77aaa1563817899d7d3f7ebcd99c96d071af38d122f2532cd05b66c`). |
| phase-66 | `DONE` | B1-CRYPTO-08 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-66/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-CRYPTO-08 row). The artifact-signer pin now binds the FULL signer set, not a "last signed entry seen" cert: `ArtifactSignatureVerifier.collectSignerSet` (`ArtifactSignatureVerifier.kt:162`) force-verifies the JAR (`JarFile(verify=true)`) and (1) rejects ANY unsigned non-META-INF entry inside an otherwise-verified jar (`:173`, the attacker-key-on-`classes.dex` shape), (2) rejects any multi-signer entry, (3) rejects any archive whose entries mix different signers (`:189`), and (4) fails hard on an EMPTY verified signer set (`:199`) — the old `certs.firstOrNull()` last-entry fallback is gone (source-pinned). "One signer" is judged PER SIGNER CHAIN, not per certificate: `singleSignerChain` (`:235`) splits the JAR verifier's leaf-first chain list on certificate boundaries (issuer-DN match AND a verifiable signature), so a single CA-issued signer (leaf + issuers) is ACCEPTED while a second signer's chain is a hard boundary (review-fix for the pre-chain code's `certs.size != 1` over-rejection). New pure-JVM `plugins/runtime/SignerCertificatePolicy.kt` is the single decision table run by `verify()` (`:115`) — after the pin compare (`:107`, so a wrong key reports the accurate pin-mismatch reason): `checkValidity(now)` rejects an expired/not-yet-valid pinned cert (previously silently accepted) and a `KeyUsage` extension lacking the digitalSignature bit (bit 0) is rejected; an absent extension is unrestricted (RFC 5280). As defense in depth, a key-usage-invalid cert is ALSO refused by the signer-set gate when the platform JAR verifier surfaces such entries with `null` certificates. Pure JVM, runs unchanged on the API 26+ floor — no new platform requirement, no fallback needed. Tests: new `B1Crypto08SignerSetTest` (19 — single-pinned-signer passes; CA-chain-signed single signer passes; two-signer jar over every entry fails; signed+unsigned mixed jar fails; unsigned artifact fails; expired cert fails even with a matching pin hash; KeyUsage-excluded cert refused; policy table accepts absent/digitalSignature usage and rejects expired/not-yet-valid/non-signing certs; synthetic `singleSignerChain`/`sameChain` decision-table tests covering the multi-chain boundary and cross-entry chain equality; source pins). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1294 total (only the 2 pre-existing `B1Plat01ReleaseSigningTest` failures, untouched `app/build.gradle.kts`/`docs/RELEASE.md` asserts documented since phase-55) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (173.7 MB debug APK SHA-256 `41f94289…`). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. |
| phase-64 | `DONE` | B1-CRYPTO-05 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-64/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B1-CRYPTO-05 row). The vault DEK is no longer silently re-keyed when a stored device wrapper becomes undecryptable: new pure-JVM `services/DekReadResult.kt` = sealed `DekReadResult` (`NoBlob` / `Unlocked(dek)` / `AuthRequired` / `KeyLost(wrapperAlias)`) + typed `KeystoreKeyLostException(message, wrapperAlias)`. `SecurityService.readDekResult()` distinguishes "no blob stored" from "blob present but its AndroidKeyStore wrapping key is lost/unreadable" (the old `readDek()` collapsed both to `null`); `getOrCreateDek` THROWS `KeystoreKeyLostException` on `KeyLost` at every mint site (with and without `allowPasswordlessMint`) and mints only from `NoBlob`, so the stored wrapper can never be overwritten by a fresh DEK and the phase-43 quarantiner is never tripped for this cause. `storeDek` stamps a non-secret `wrapperAlias` (`noteflow_dek_key` / `noteflow_dek_key_auth`) + `wrapperVersion = 1` marker persisted by `SharedPrefsDekDeviceStore` (`dek_wrapper_alias`/`dek_wrapper_version`, dropped on `clear()`). `NoteflowViewModel`: new `_keystoreKeyLost` StateFlow gated into `dbGate` (`combine(_authenticated, _corruptionBlocked, _keystoreKeyLost)`); passwordless init routes through `readDekResult` (`Unlocked`→use, `NoBlob`→mint, `AuthRequired`/`KeyLost`→recovery state, the old `var dek = readDek(); if (dek==null) mint()` collapse is gone); `initializeData` catch surfaces key-lost (not corruption) when the corruption flag is clear; `setMasterPassword` throws `KeystoreKeyLostException` on `KeyLost`; new `attemptKeystoreKeyLostRecoveryFromBackup` (validates backup password BEFORE closing, mints a fresh DEK in memory, persists the device wrapper ONLY AFTER a successful restore) + `startFreshAfterKeystoreKeyLoss` (moves the old vault aside as `noteflow.sqlite.keystore-lost-<ts>`, bytes preserved) via `quarantineVaultFiles`. `MainActivity` renders the dedicated `KeystoreKeyLostScreen` between the corruption and restore screens (restore-from-backup with backup-password field + explicit two-step start-fresh). No DB schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. Tests: new `B1Crypto05SilentRekeyTest` (16 — behavioral via the `DekDeviceStore` seam + source pins). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1255 total (+16, no regressions) with only the 2 pre-existing `B1Plat01ReleaseSigningTest` failures; `gradle assembleDebug` green (APK SHA-256 `8ff42d828428c055ee37fd93556636f869d1932bdf3584fde5b71c20be929599`). |

